This project has difference from The Movies App by working with fragments instead of activities.
1. Use of MainActivity: only used to create and set fragments instead of connection of components logic.
    The components connection logic is inside the fragments classes.
2. Getting application parameter in a fragment class: requireActivity().getApplication()
2b. When observing LiveData in fragments, use getViewLifecyclerOwner() instead of requireActivity() as parameter.
3. Getting owner class parameter in a fragment class: this (same as in an activity class)
4. Creating viewModel instance using ViewModelProvider when AllNewsViewModel has two parameters:
    By default, ViewModelProvider takes only application. To make it take two parameters: application and newsRepository, create a custom class named AllNewsViewModelFactory
    Then initialize application , newsRepository, factory and then create viewModel in AllNewsFragment.
5. Don't use DataBindingUtil.setContentView() in onViewCreated as it will destroy activity and just load fragment. But fragment lives inside activity so crash.
    Instead use
    fragmentAllNewsBinding = DataBindingUtil.inflate(inflater, R.layout.fragment_all_news, container, false);
    return fragmentAllNewsBinding.getRoot();
    these in OnCreateView only.
6. Images if not available, I use a placeholder image in News.java
7. write android:usesCleartextTraffic="true" in manifests so that images with http:// can also be opened. without it, only https:// loads.
8. MainActivity: 43
    An activity does not know which fragment/s are on top of it. To get reference to a fragement, use getSupportFragmentManager() as it is a manager of fragments.
    findFragmentById(): pass parameter of the root layout: like frameLayout since a fragment is associated to its root level layouts.
9. Tell the fragment that it has a menu inside onCreate of AllNewsFragement
    put onCreateOptionsMenu() and onOptionsItemSelected() inside AllNewsFragment.
10. Even after setting menu, it is not visible since there is no container to hold it on top of screen. Due to NoActionBar set in themes.xml
    Add MaterialToolBar in activity_main and findViewById for toolbar in MainActivity

11. Important: instead of using height = 56dp, use height = ?attr/actionBarSize. This will look in theme and set height as defined std height of actionBar. works dynamically for diff. devices.
12. wrote setSupportActionBar(toolbar) and found view by id inside MainActivity instead of AllNewsFragment. Reason:
    declare toolbare in mainactivity but menu ko set ko allnewsFragment hi kr rha. So ok.
13. Use @Ignore with properties you don't want to show in room db.
15. To get back from a fragment, use ft.addToBackStack(null); (ft is fragmentTransaction)
16. How to send data like intents using args and startActivity(i) with fragments: see NewsItemClickHandler and newsDetails
17. How to use webview to load urls inside app and not external browser: see newsDetails and layout for it.
